{# THE ORGANIZATION'S INCIDENTS OVERVIEW — the strip across every area the
   module is switched on in, and what needs somebody as the banner above it.

   EVERY FIGURE IS THE AREAS' OWN, ADDED: the area overview's figures, read
   area by area and summed by IncidentOrgService. #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiIncident/org/base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Incidents · {{ scope.label }}{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}Every incident filed in every area, newest first, at organization scope.{% endblock %}

{% block incident_org_page %}
    {%- set late = summary.pastTerm -%}
    {%- if late is not empty -%}
        {%- set n = late|length -%}
        {%- set k = summary.pastTermAreas -%}
        {%- set shown = late|slice(0, 4) -%}
        {%- set cause = shown|map(row => row.incident.reference ~ ' in ' ~ row.area.name)|join('; ') ~ (n > shown|length ? ', and ' ~ (n - shown|length) ~ ' more' : '') -%}
        {{ include('@Shell/_banner.html.twig', {
            title: n ~ ' open past ' ~ (n == 1 ? 'its' : 'their') ~ ' term, in ' ~ k ~ ' area' ~ (k == 1 ? '' : 's'),
            text: cause,
            actions: {'Incidents': path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Incident\\Controller\\IncidentOrgController::LIST_ROUTE'), scope.areaUuid ? {area: scope.areaUuid} : {})},
        }, with_context: false) }}
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="factband">
        <span class="f" data-fact="areas"><span class="k">Areas</span><span class="v">{{ summary.areas }}<em>{{ summary.areas > 0 and summary.reporting == summary.areas ? 'all reporting' : summary.reporting ~ ' reporting' }}</em></span></span>
        <span class="f" data-fact="filed"><span class="k">Filed in {{ summary.month|date('F')|lower }}</span><span class="v">{{ summary.filed }}<em>{{ scope.isOrganization ? 'org-wide' : scope.label }}</em></span></span>
        <span class="f" data-fact="in-progress"><span class="k">In progress</span><span class="v">{{ summary.inProgress }}<em>across {{ summary.inProgressAreas }} area{{ summary.inProgressAreas == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</em></span></span>
        <span class="f" data-fact="critical"><span class="k">Critical open</span><span class="v">{{ summary.criticalOpen }}<em>{% for name, count in summary.criticalByArea %}{{ name }} {{ count }}{% if not loop.last %} &middot; {% endif %}{% else %}none open{% endfor %}</em></span></span>
        <span class="sp"></span>
        <span class="more" style="color:var(--dim)">Settings are the area&rsquo;s</span>
    </div>

    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab">The organization-level incidents<span class="src">&middot; three tabs</span></span>
        <div class="rln"><span>Same tabs as the area module</span><span class="mono d">Overview &middot; Incidents &middot; Incident kinds &mdash; read across all areas</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>One taxonomy, {{ summary.areas }} area{{ summary.areas == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</span><span class="mono d">kinds are the organization&rsquo;s, so a category means the same thing in every area and the register can be read down a single column</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>The lists are the area&rsquo;s</span><span class="mono d">species, methods and named places stay per-area; the org register shows the value and names the area it came from</span></div>
        <div class="use" style="margin-bottom:0"><b>Nothing here is a second incidents module.</b> It is the same register with the area filter widened, which is the only way the two can never disagree.</div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
